    {
      "id": "event-contract",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": 1790,
        "y": -1526
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Contract",
        "body": "- An event key names the event; the port is `event:<key>`, an output on the emitter.\n- The `invokes` edge class: any source, a Method as target. Drawn from the event's port on a node, or on the graph's root.\n- A class declares its events in `nodeDef.defaults.events`, and a node made from the class carries them. There is no class-wide trigger: wire the node, or use the root's `graph.changed`.\n- Changes are announced by `changeAnnouncements`, from both write paths: `GraphCrud` updates and the `nodeUpdate` event. A new write path must call it, and a UI never emits these events itself.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
