    {
      "id": "event-known-gaps",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Known gaps",
      "position": {
        "x": -910,
        "y": -1166
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Known gaps",
        "body": "- Events do not cross a graph. There is no event over a Bridge and no wildcard subscription, by design.\n- The shape of an event's payload is declared only as a `payloadContract` on a class's event, and is not checked on delivery.\n- A `listens` edge class still exists in canon. It appears to belong to the older Event Handler model; the runtime follows `invokes`. It needs retiring or explaining.\n- A Method's declared effects are enforced for fewer operations than they can name; see Method.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Rule"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592070381,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
